  "location": "46 CFR parts 501, 503, 504, 508, 535, 545, 560",
  "text": {
    "en": {
      "title": "Federal Maritime Commission: 8 references to former U.S. Code sections or former act names",
      "summary": "In the CFR chapters assigned to the Federal Maritime Commission, 8 references in 7 sections use a former address or name: 6 cite a renumbered section; 2 cite a section replaced by a new one when the title was enacted as positive law. Each reference was compared with release point 119-134 of the U.S. Code, which names where the old number went.",
      "impact": "A reader who follows these references finds a note that the section moved, or no section, instead of the text. A reference to a moved section may keep its legal effect, but the address no longer leads to the text. No effect on a decision or an amount has been established.",
      "correction": "The agency decides how to update each reference. Where the U.S. Code names the section the old number moved to, the evidence below gives it."
    }
  },
